    {
      "path": "experiments/registry-overrides/adaptive-power-terra-20261102/adaptive-type4-control-61742.json",
      "sha256": "5a39c457cc12d8d0b7ce8afc818bf4cd3f254eebdb4da6c553ca981581a6bfc6",
      "findings": [
        "A801 GET and E802 SET use size 0x404 attribute packets: u32 count at +0 and 16-byte entries at +4; each row contains u16 type +0, u16 role +2, u16 attribute +4, u16 flags +6, u32 value +8. Type4 selects the auxiliary object at LPWR parent+12C8. Source current GRPG implementation already queries type4 attribute9 roles 0..10 and checks unchanged opaque bytes and per-row validity.",
        "A801 type4 first requires object+5C nonzero and 8F5EC0 further requires role low byte <11 and the corresponding support bit in +5C. Attribute9 returns support value1 for a valid role. Unsupported role is an invalid row, not a valid value0. Attribute10 invokes 8F5960 and returns 1 iff the selected reason DWORD aux+role*0x80+0x68 is zero, else 0. The inspected getter dispatch does not expose that reason DWORD directly.",
        "E802 type4 dispatches 8F61F0, accepts attribute10 only. Value0 sets bit1 in the selected reason DWORD; if the prior DWORD was zero it may call B9C340 (firmware 00/03/0D) and for role1 additionally invokes GPU+2120 virtual+598. Nonzero clears bit1 only; if that makes the complete reason DWORD zero it invokes B9C420 (firmware 02/03/0C). It leaves other reason bits intact. If reason DWORD already zero, the clear operation is a no-op. These are shared bit operations, not counted or per-client references; an enabled predicate change does not identify an owner.",
        "Source-initialized controller-to-auxiliary role association via group row+F2: GR controller0 -> role0, MS controller4 -> role2, NVDEC12 -> role4, NVENC13 -> role5, OFA14 -> role7, NVJPG15 -> role6. Controller10/11 initialize row+F2 to 11, outside supported range. These are construction-path associations; device capabilities and runtime validity must be read independently.",
        "A bounded read-only probe may adapt existing _bit1_request/_bit1_roles packet for type4 attribute9 plus matching attribute10 rows for exact roles 0,2,4,5,6,7, preserving packet routing/opaque fields and interpreting invalid rows as unavailable. If enabled=1 it establishes reason DWORD is zero at that read, not ownership or physical gating. This is a read-only candidate; no SET or hardware performed."
      ],
